  "findings": [
    "No sign/transpose/indexing/block/channel-reassignment error was identified in these checks; this does not certify upstream voltage processing.",
    "Provider analysis evaluates300ms trial-window mean vectors after nested-CV trial-onset reaction-time offset0..1s and excludes near-target trials; V2 evaluates20ms instantaneous unit direction throughout go periods. Trial-onset reaction time is not a neural-to-target lag shift.",
    "Provider TX features are centered over each whole block; SBP uses whole-block median and whole-session robust scale. Those normalizers would use future observations if copied into streaming evaluation.",
    "TX4.5 is highly sparse in the exposed earliest T3/T6 sessions. SBP is available but has markedly different numerical scales across people. This motivates a fixed feature/normalization hypothesis, not a measured causal explanation of V2 failure.",
    "Target-minus-cursor is a closed-loop intention proxy, not measured limb velocity. Channel IDs are local to each participant. Task coordinate scales differ; uniform scale cancels in a unit vector."
  ],
